# Renaming fragments

Rename uses the shared symbol planner, so only explicit fragment names change.
Validation rejects ambiguous definitions, collisions and changes to root status
without touching prose, filenames or generated output.

The provider returns a proposed workspace edit; it does not apply edits or write
generated files itself. VS Code owns applying the edit. A resulting literate
content-change event can then trigger the ordinary generation path.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Author
    participant VS as VS Code
    participant Provider as Rename provider
    participant Repo as Fragment repository
    participant Planner as Symbol planner
    User->>VS: Rename a fragment
    VS->>Provider: Prepare rename at cursor
    Provider->>Repo: Refresh from current buffers
    Repo-->>Provider: Exact occurrence and source snapshot
    Provider->>Planner: Validate same-name plan
    Planner-->>Provider: Unique valid definition
    Provider-->>VS: Inner-name range and placeholder
    User->>VS: Enter new name
    VS->>Provider: Request rename edits
    Provider->>Repo: Refresh again
    Provider->>Planner: Plan rename from fresh sources
    Note over Planner: Validate names, collisions and Markdown structure
    alt Valid plan
        Planner-->>Provider: Name-only edit ranges
        Provider-->>VS: WorkspaceEdit
        VS->>VS: Apply edits to source documents
        VS->>Repo: Literate content-change events
    else Unsafe rename
        Planner-->>Provider: Validation error
        Provider-->>VS: Reject rename without partial edits
    end
```

Cancellation and positions that do not identify a defined fragment stop before
returning edits. Those early exits are omitted here to keep the successful
interaction and validation failure visible.

``` ts : <<rename provider class>>=
export class LiterateRenameProvider implements vscode.RenameProvider
{
    constructor(public readonly repository : FragmentRepository) {}

    <<prepare fragment rename>>
    <<fragment rename provider>>
}
```

Preparing a rename refreshes the read-only repository from open buffers. The
shared lookup supplies the inner name range, excluding the tag delimiters.
A no-op plan also verifies that the selected symbol has one base definition.

``` ts : <<prepare fragment rename>>=
public async prepareRename(
    document : vscode.TextDocument,
    position : vscode.Position,
    token : vscode.CancellationToken
)
{
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    const workspaceFolder = determineWorkspaceFolder(document);
    if(!workspaceFolder) { return null; }
    await this.repository.processLiterateFiles(document);
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    const location = this.repository.getFragmentTagLocation(
        document, document.lineAt(position.line), position
    );
    if(!location.valid || !location.fragment) { return null; }
    planFragmentRename(
        this.repository.getSourceDocuments(workspaceFolder), location.name, location.name
    );
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    return { range: location.rangeExclusive, placeholder: location.name };
}
```

The actual request refreshes again: the user may have edited a buffer since
preparation. Cancellation discards the whole result, never a partial edit set.
Planner errors propagate to the editor as actionable rename failures.

``` ts : <<fragment rename provider>>=
public async provideRenameEdits(
    document : vscode.TextDocument,
    position : vscode.Position,
    newName : string,
    token : vscode.CancellationToken
)
{
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    const workspaceFolder = determineWorkspaceFolder(document);
    if(!workspaceFolder) { return null; }
    await this.repository.processLiterateFiles(document);
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    const location = this.repository.getFragmentTagLocation(
        document, document.lineAt(position.line), position
    );
    if(!location.valid || !location.fragment) { return null; }
    const plan = planFragmentRename(
        this.repository.getSourceDocuments(workspaceFolder), location.name, newName
    );
    <<adapt fragment rename plan>>
}
```

Planner paths are canonical workspace-relative source paths. Convert their
UTF-16 name ranges to editor edits without reading disk or applying changes.

``` ts : <<adapt fragment rename plan>>=
const workspaceEdit = new vscode.WorkspaceEdit();
for(const edit of plan)
{
    if(token.isCancellationRequested) { return null; }
    workspaceEdit.replace(
        vscode.Uri.joinPath(workspaceFolder.uri, edit.path),
        new vscode.Range(edit.line, edit.startColumn, edit.line, edit.endColumn),
        edit.newText
    );
}
return token.isCancellationRequested ? null : workspaceEdit;
```
